    {
      "id": "task-collection-introduction",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Tasks remain tasks",
      "position": { "x": 0, "y": -40 },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 250,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "ports": [
        { "id": "root", "label": "root", "direction": "bidirectional", "dataType": "any", "angle": 210 },
        { "id": "top", "label": "top", "direction": "bidirectional", "dataType": "value", "angle": 270 },
        { "id": "right", "label": "right", "direction": "bidirectional", "dataType": "value", "angle": 0 },
        { "id": "bottom", "label": "bottom", "direction": "bidirectional", "dataType": "value", "angle": 90 },
        { "id": "left", "label": "left", "direction": "bidirectional", "dataType": "value", "angle": 180 }
      ],
      "style": { "background": "#172033", "color": "#e2e8f0", "border": "2px solid #334155", "borderRadius": 24, "padding": 20 },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Tasks remain tasks\n\nA task is a regular task inside its own graph and when projected into another graph. **Project** describes scope and point of view—not a separate semantic type.\n\nLocal tasks live here. A task that needs its own subtasks, questions, decisions, risks, or durable summary may own a graph and appear here through a portal.",
        "identity": { "graphId": "michael-task-collection" }
      }
    },
